Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 18:03:58 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Routing: per-goal budgets, timeout and SoftFail fixes;
 queue cancel fixes

Behind VMFeatures.RoutingFixes (default on):
- AttemptRoute refills Timeout and Retries and clears WaitTime for each
  goal. They were set once per routing frame, so after one long wait
  every later goal started with an empty allowance.
- The wait-timeout branch clears WaitTime after giving up a goal. It
  used to leave WaitTime > 0 with Timeout <= 0, so each following tick
  gave up the next goal and the whole route failed within a few ticks.
- SoftFail moves to the INITIAL state for the next goal, so portals,
  chairs and standing up are handled. Staying in WALKING made the Sim
  walk straight at the next goal's position.
- VMSlotParser can report WallInWay (it was missing from the fail
  priority list); collision give-ups blame the avatar or object in the
  way instead of the routing Sim; RouteResult is cleared on success.

Behind VMFeatures.QueueFixes (default on):
- TS1 interactions flagged "allow dogs" (same bit as TSO's MustRun) can
  be cancelled while queued; cancelling one used to cancel the running
  action instead.
- TS1 queue skipping after inserting a higher priority action no longer
  loops forever when an item can't be removed (ParentIdle/ParentExit).

